WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.168 --> 00:00:01.965
- I don't know where my tongue belongs.

00:00:04.623 --> 00:00:07.433
I feel like it doesn't touch
any part of my mouth, somehow.

00:00:14.965 --> 00:00:17.272
- I've never seen letters that do that.

00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:19.895
- I feel like Polish is a
(clears throat) language, right?

00:00:19.895 --> 00:00:20.643
- "Shet".

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:21.485
- "Chet-um".

00:00:21.485 --> 00:00:24.060
- "Shell-tru-um".

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:24.856
- "Chaim".

00:00:24.856 --> 00:00:25.528
- Chelm?

00:00:26.147 --> 00:00:27.106
- But there's a T.

00:00:27.106 --> 00:00:30.073
- That's not a T, that's an
L with a cross through it?

00:00:32.362 --> 00:00:33.908
- Nope, not gonna get this one.

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:35.111
- That A's got a dick!

00:00:35.111 --> 00:00:36.248
- "Groot-squids".

00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:37.667
- "Grood-zee-gots".

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.249
- "Grood-zee-odds".

00:00:39.249 --> 00:00:40.416
- "Grood-goz".

00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:41.655
- Grudziadz?

00:00:42.284 --> 00:00:44.131
- Oh, that's much
"Frenchier" than I thought.

00:00:46.503 --> 00:00:47.884
- Okay, this one looks like it has

00:00:47.884 --> 00:00:49.678
- more of the made-up letters.

00:00:49.678 --> 00:00:52.678
- Not made up, they're
Polish, that's theirs.

00:00:52.678 --> 00:00:53.811
- What do they sound like?

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:57.018
- (honks, laughs)

00:00:57.018 --> 00:00:58.551
- "Wow-wack".

00:00:58.551 --> 00:00:59.982
- "La-tock-ick".

00:00:59.982 --> 00:01:01.221
- "Lock-loo-eck"?

00:01:01.221 --> 00:01:03.313
- (laughs) What? "Wook-suave-eck"?

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:06.520
- See, now I've learned
that W's really a V,

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.194
- and that's something I should have known

00:01:07.194 --> 00:01:08.241
- from the beginning.

00:01:10.525 --> 00:01:11.450
- I just get thrown when they

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.276
- throw all those consonants together.

00:01:13.276 --> 00:01:15.319
- I'm gonna guess that the
R does not make a sound

00:01:15.319 --> 00:01:17.319
- and that it's "Zes-zow".

00:01:17.319 --> 00:01:18.284
- "Rue-jew".

00:01:18.284 --> 00:01:19.204
- "Res-oh".

00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:20.670
- "Er-zez-ow".

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:24.259
- "Rez-is-zwah" (laughs).

00:01:24.956 --> 00:01:26.129
- Rzeszow.

00:01:26.129 --> 00:01:27.999
- I appreciate the use of Z's,

00:01:27.999 --> 00:01:30.015
- because we don't use Z's enough.

00:01:32.556 --> 00:01:33.391
- "Shush-sho-vah".

00:01:33.391 --> 00:01:35.219
- "Jiz-stock-on-wah".

00:01:35.219 --> 00:01:36.515
- "Jesh-stock-ah-wah".

00:01:36.515 --> 00:01:38.465
- "Zes-osh-uah", "Zes-osh-uh-vah".

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.732
- How does it sound?

00:01:41.888 --> 00:01:42.928
- No.

00:01:42.928 --> 00:01:44.609
- Czeestochowa?

00:01:47.022 --> 00:01:49.144
- This looks like just
something you pulled out

00:01:49.144 --> 00:01:51.063
- of a bag of Scrabble,
like you just reached in

00:01:51.063 --> 00:01:52.486
- and pulled out a bunch
of letters and you're like,

00:01:52.486 --> 00:01:53.403
- well, I'm (bleeped).

00:01:53.403 --> 00:01:56.412
- S-Z-C-Z sound is one that escapes me.

00:01:56.412 --> 00:01:58.250
- "Bid-duh-gah-zvzvzvzv".

00:01:58.697 --> 00:02:00.789
- "Bid-gah-shhhzzz".

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:01.908
- "Bid-go-shhhzzz".

00:02:01.908 --> 00:02:03.294
- Bydgoszcz.

00:02:03.294 --> 00:02:04.788
- It's got its own echo.

00:02:07.311 --> 00:02:08.873
- See now, this is a short one,

00:02:08.873 --> 00:02:10.166
- but I know it's gonna throw me.

00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:11.589
- This looks like this word was tried

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:13.380
- to be crossed out, like, three times.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.345
- This is how they say LOLZ, right?

00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:17.639
- This looks fun.

00:02:19.094 --> 00:02:21.429
- I'm just gonna have
fun with this one, "luz".

00:02:21.429 --> 00:02:22.564
- "Lodz".

00:02:22.564 --> 00:02:23.686
- "Wah-duh-z".

00:02:24.763 --> 00:02:26.067
- "Yez".

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:31.067
- (laughs) Lodz, that's my favorite.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.599
- "Wads-ah-wah".

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:37.159
- "Wars-wars-ow-wuh".

00:02:37.159 --> 00:02:38.065
- "War-zhav-uh".

00:02:38.065 --> 00:02:40.531
- "Was-ah-wah-wah-wah-wah"
(laughs) does it repeat?

00:02:40.531 --> 00:02:41.748
- "Wars-va-va".

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.127
- Warszawa.

00:02:44.127 --> 00:02:46.289
- It makes a little more sense now,

00:02:47.427 --> 00:02:49.306
- when you tell me what the symbols do.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:53.502
- All right, you won, Poland, you won.

00:02:54.338 --> 00:02:55.556
- [Voiceover] I like the
letters you're bringing

00:02:55.556 --> 00:02:57.261
into the game, these
ones I've never heard of,

00:02:57.261 --> 00:03:02.014
like the (mumbling), I don't
know how to pronounce it yet,

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:02.853
I'll get there.

00:03:02.853 --> 00:03:05.397
- Do widzenia, what's that?

00:03:07.326 --> 00:03:08.660
Do widzenia.

